---
import BrandMark from "../components/BrandMark.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Public team notebook</p>
        <h1 id="home-title">Kernel Kittens</h1>
        <p class="lede">CTF write-ups, competition history, and work we can actually show.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">We play CTFs and publish the useful parts once the rules allow it.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button-link" href="/writeups/">Read the archive</a>
          <a class="button-link button-link--quiet" href="/certifications/">Check the record</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-mark">
        <BrandMark decorative={true} class="hero-mark__svg" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Write-ups</p>
          <h2 id="work-title">Proof, when it can be public.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Event rules come first. Finished solutions stay private until there is a clear basis to publish them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="empty-state">
        <span class="empty-state__index" aria-hidden="true">00</span>
        <div>
          <h3>No public write-ups yet.</h3>
          <p>Seven confirmed BushBash solves are ready, but the event rules still block publication. They stay private until that changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="record-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Team record</p>
          <h2 id="record-title">Claims with labels.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Current credentials, previous credentials, and earlier team results stay clearly separated.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="record-grid">
        <article class="record-card">
          <span class="record-card__label">Current</span>
          <h3>Google Cybersecurity Professional Certificate</h3>
          <p>Held by a Kernel Kittens team member.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="record-card">
          <span class="record-card__label">Prior team result</span>
          <h3>Cyber Apocalypse 2026</h3>
          <p>12th of 6,744 teams with 1337_PwnSp4c3.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="record-card">
          <span class="record-card__label">Publication rule</span>
          <h3>No fake proof.</h3>
          <p>No invented roster, recycled flags, or credentials presented without their real status.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
